This distribution contains Bearer 2.1.0 modified by Lomo CodeSecurity.
Upstream: https://github.com/Bearer/bearer
Upstream source commit: 814948ecc198a743b13a75a6bfd4688514285220
Intended modified version: 2.1.0+lomo.1

The cumulative lomo.patch preserves Python subscription tuple keys, avoids
unnecessary trace formatting, preserves empty detector/cache results, skips
unreachable outer pattern conjunction branches and adds bounded empty-result
reuse for one verified immutable auxiliary-rule closure. It includes semantic,
cycle, cancellation, scope, immutable-context and actual-reuse regressions.
A completed empty traversal now also proves its visited children/alias closure,
using a separate bounded pending bitset; incomplete or positive traversals
publish no proof. Negative external-alias and invalidation tests cover reuse.
One exact generated JavaScript statement-pair query collects candidate second
siblings and materializes its original captures on demand, avoiding eager
quadratic storage. Native-query differential tests cover capture order,
cardinality, nested blocks, comments, Unicode and malformed source.
The completed AST indexes collected raw queries. Shared rules with no possible
query matches, and auxiliary root-variable patterns whose first bound reference
is proven empty, avoid redundant traversal. Proofs use compiled structure, with
bounded acyclic references and sanitizer, active-execution and unknown-shape
fallbacks. Differential tests preserve positive findings, missing-variable
errors, cancellation and the reachability of later filters.
The validated installation lane scales the computed per-file analysis duration
once by 1, 5.2 or 7.8 for Mac, Linux or Windows/WSL under D-021.
Independent native whole-scan caps are 600, 1560 or 2340 seconds.
Unset retains upstream timing;
unknown lanes fail before discovery. This does not alter memory/source bounds,
worker cleanup grace or incomplete-report rejection. Boundary-size and invalid
factor controls cover assignment.
Private phase, query, rule-work and CPU diagnostic probes are not included.

